Return to Permissive?
Protections removed at the next start:
Your own settings from config apply instead of each of these.
• Sandbox: write only in the current folder (where the Corbanu home and the
    nested-launch registry stay read-only): no extra writable folders, no /tmp
    or $TMPDIR; approved commands stay inside it too; escalation and permission-
    request tools are off; the project's .git, .codex and .agents stay read-
    only, even with Grant once (it only lets one command write a core.hooksPath
    hooks folder and, in your home folder, start-up files); reading credential
    files (.env, .env.* and .envrc files, also ones created later, on Windows
    from the next command on; not .env.example, .env.sample or .env.template;
    SSH, cloud and CLI tokens) or Corbanu's sign-in, vault, config and history
    is denied to agent commands and is never granted, not even once (switch to
    Permissive in /security to allow it); on Linux a command is stopped when
    such a file appears while it runs, and a process already waiting for that
    file can read it in the moment before the stop; a credential file that is a
    link must be replaced with a regular file or moved out of the folder
• Approvals: untrusted: you approve every command that is not known read-only
    (reviewer: you, never auto-review)
• Network: off for agent commands; web search off
• Vault: the vault store and sign-in file are unreadable to agent commands, and
    direct `corbanu vault …` commands are refused; secret-like environment
    variables (KEY, SECRET, TOKEN, VAULT, PASSWORD, PASSPHRASE, CREDENTIAL) are
    removed, and with secretless_agent_launch on so is every other variable
    outside an allowlist (for example PATH, HOME, locale, terminal, proxy and
    tool locations; set others explicitly in shell_environment_policy.set);
    login profiles and shell snapshots are not used
• Model keys: provider API keys from the environment or the vault are held by
    the isolated credential broker, which sends model requests for Corbanu
    (sign-in tokens are passed to it; command, AWS and header sign-ins are not
    brokered; realtime and websockets are off); if it cannot start, model
    requests are refused, never sent directly (broker_model_auth;
    `broker_model_auth = false` in your own config keeps it off)
• Child agents: spawned agents get the same values; custom roles that would
    change them are refused at start; Claude panes are refused because Claude
    Code runs outside the sandbox, unless contained_external_agents and
    secretless_agent_launch run them in it, asking you before every command,
    file edit and web request (reading files stays automatic) (Claude Code sign-
    in still runs)
• Nested agents: agent commands can start other agents (`corbanu exec`,
    `review`, `resume`, `fork`, a new session, `app-server` or `mcp-server`)
    without Aggressive enforced
Your own approval, sandbox, network, web search and environment settings from
config apply again exactly as saved. The Aggressive vault rule file is removed
at the next start.
Takes effect when you restart Corbanu Terminal; this session stays Aggressive
until then, and its pending approvals end with it.
